alternation that the model linearly rewards (model over-produces choosing perfect alternation), above null the reverse.\nimport numpy as np' perfect_alternator_choice_rate '\ndef test_statistic(df):\n    fa, fb = _feat(df, lambda s: float(_sw(s) == len(s) - 1))\n    return _rate_choose_higher(df, fa, fb, np.ones(len(df), bool))'\n\nw '# name: more_switches_among_high_switch_pairs\n# description: Among pairs where both sequences switch on at least 60% of transitions and switch rates differ, the rate of choosing the more-switching sequence; observed below null means the alternation preference saturates/inverts at high switch rates (inverted-U) while the linear model over-produces it.\nimport numpy as np' more_switches_among_high_switch_pairs '\ndef test_statistic(df):\n    fa, fb = _feat(df, lambda s: _sw(s) / (len(s) - 1))\n    return _rate_choose_higher(df, fa, fb, (fa >= 0.6) & (fb >= 0.6))'\n\nw '# name: more_distinct_triplets_at_equal_switches\n# description: Among pairs with equal switch counts but different numbers of distinct length-3 substrings, the rate of choosing the sequence with more distinct triplets; observed above null means people reward local pattern variety that span and switching miss (model under-produces it).\nimport numpy as np' more_distinct_triplets_at_equal_switches '\ndef test_statistic(df):\n    sa, sb = _feat(df, _sw)\n    ta, tb = _feat(df, lambda s: float(len({s[i:i+3] for i in range(len(s) - 2)})))\n    return _rate_choose_higher(df, ta, tb, sa == sb)'\n\nw '# name: more_heads_choice_rate\n# description: Among pairs whose head counts differ, the rate of choosing the sequence with more H; observed away from the null mean means an H-versus-T asymmetry the symmetric span/switch model cannot produce (above: model under-produces a heads preference; below: tails preference).\nimport numpy as np' more_heads_choice_rate '\ndef test_statistic(df):\n    fa, fb = _feat(df, lambda s: float(s.count(\"H\")))\n    return _rate_choose_higher(df, fa, fb, np.ones(len(df), bool))'\n\nw '# name: switch_preference_long_minus_short\n# description: Rate of choosing the more-switching sequence on length-8 pairs minus that rate on pairs of length <=7; observed above null means the alternation preference grows with length more than the model (whose switch weight ignores length) predicts, below null that it shrinks.\nimport numpy as np' switch_preference_long_minus_short '\ndef test_statistic(df):\n    fa, fb = _feat(df, lambda s: _sw(s) / (len(s) - 1))\n    L = df[\"sequence_a\"].str.len().to_numpy()\n    return _rate_choose_higher(df, fa, fb, L == 8) - _rate_choose_higher(df, fa, fb, L <= 7)'\n\nw '# name: late_minus_early_streak_avoidance\n# description: Rate of choosing the sequence with the shorter longest run in the second half of each session minus the first half (trial_index split at the participant median); observed away from null (~0) means streak avoidance changes over the session, which the static model cannot produce (below null: it weakens late).\nimport numpy as np' late_minus_early_streak_avoidance '\ndef test_statistic(df):\n    ra, rb = _feat(df, _run)\n    t = df[\"trial_index\"].to_numpy(dtype=float)\n    med = df.groupby(\"participant_id\")[\"trial_index\"].transform(\"median\").to_numpy(dtype=float)\n    return _rate_choose_higher(df, -ra, -rb, t > med) - _rate_choose_higher(df, -ra, -rb, t <= med)'\n\nw '# name: participant_streak_avoidance_variance\n# description: Variance across participants of their rate of choosing the sequence with the shorter longest run (pairs differing in longest run); observed above null means individual differences in streak aversion exceed what personal span ideals and switching weights produce.\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd' participant_streak_avoidance_variance '\ndef test_statistic(df):\n    ra, rb = _feat(df, _run)\n    y = df[\"chose_left\"].to_numpy()\n    m = ra != rb\n    c = np.where(ra[m] < rb[m], y[m], 1 - y[m])\n    return float(pd.Series(c).groupby(