tion term, so these test whether the switching term here accounts for the effect.\n- **`late_minus_early_streak_avoidance` and `participant_streak_avoidance_variance`** both survived the FDR correction against `tally_span_personal_ideal` in iter 2. They are repeated because the new model adds a person-specific switching weight, which might absorb the second one.\n\nEach file's `# description:` line says which direction relative to the null mean means the model under- or over-produces the effect."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4112,"cache_read_input_tokens":45985,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4112,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9a431828-2b9c-4229-b8db-1b0d7022afef","uuid":"bcc22d24-1f94-439a-9c83-aad00c645080","timestamp":"2026-10-03T13:46:37.553Z","request_id":"req_011CffQXMgysr2QCEG42CRp5"}
